    "summary": "I built four full bases in a straight row at (0,0), (1,0), (2,0) and (3,0), split into two pairs. The bases at (0,0) and (1,0) are pair A, joined by joint bolt jointBolt:0#0,0#0. The bases at (2,0) and (3,0) are pair B, joined by joint bolt jointBolt:0#2,0#0. A double side connector (connector:0#1,0|2,0) across the seam between (1,0) and (2,0) is the only thing joining the two pairs.\n\nI capped the open faces with 18 solid end caps. I deliberately skipped the lockJoints house rule: it would have put a joint bolt between the pairs, which the brief rules out. The first joint bolt raised a LOOSE_BODY warning when it went on, before the other parts were added. The final check came back with no issues, and the mesh-collision check is clear. That leaves 23 parts in total. I didn't add any props because the brief isn't about a use.",
    "outcome": "built"
  },
